  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186124474,
      "id": "149fa184-850f-52d8-a309-4b79a371a74d",
      "title": "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given a Description"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "71a6d118-fdce-57b0-a146-2c69a2a5dcf7",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x)=|x-4|+6,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-\\infty,3]$\n- **II.** $x\\in (3,\\infty)$\n- **III.** $x\\in (4,6]$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The graph of the function $f(x)=|x-4|+6$ can be obtained in the following way:\n\n- Take the curve $y=|x|.$\n\n- Translate it by $4$ units to the right,  to get $y=|x-4|.$\n\n- Finally, translate $y=|x-4|$ by $6$ units up to get $f(x)=|x-4|+6.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186124474/plots/362cb383749702e379e706040906e343dbb0fb4431863c238e0f5e1834f300b4-0.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in (-\\infty,3]$ and $x\\in (4,6].$ On these intervals, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186124474/plots/362cb383749702e379e706040906e343dbb0fb4431863c238e0f5e1834f300b4-1.png)\n\n  \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not invertible on the interval $x\\in (3,\\infty).$ On this interval, some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186124474/plots/362cb383749702e379e706040906e343dbb0fb4431863c238e0f5e1834f300b4-2.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\".",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "967ed434-1bf2-5678-82f2-fd17b7291ed3",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
