  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186124474,
      "id": "149fa184-850f-52d8-a309-4b79a371a74d",
      "title": "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given a Description"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "23926d50-b08f-55d9-8865-108649952d04",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x)=(x-1)^{2}-1,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-\\infty,1]$\n\n- **II.** $x\\in (1,\\infty)$\n\n- **III.** $x\\in (-1,3]$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The graph of the function $f(x)=(x-1)^{2}-1$ can be obtained in the following way:\n\n1\\. Take the curve $y={x}^{2}.$\n\n2\\. Translate it by $1$ units to the right,  to get $y=(x-1)^{2}.$\n\n3\\. Finally, translate $y=(x-1)^{2}$  by $1$ unit down to get $f(x)=(x-1)^{2}-1.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186124474/plots/00c28aedcd604bb7a115be35e47b77a70a95e28ada62ea5bdb0834f6bbb34ce9-0.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in (-\\infty,1]$ and $x\\in (1,\\infty).$ On these intervals, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186124474/plots/00c28aedcd604bb7a115be35e47b77a70a95e28ada62ea5bdb0834f6bbb34ce9-1.png)\n\n  \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not invertible on the interval $x\\in (-1,3].$ On this interval, some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186124474/plots/00c28aedcd604bb7a115be35e47b77a70a95e28ada62ea5bdb0834f6bbb34ce9-2.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\".",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "56a3081e-063d-5be7-a012-dab304749a41",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
