    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186124474,
      "id": "149fa184-850f-52d8-a309-4b79a371a74d",
      "title": "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given a Description"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "c9bc4a93-422c-5f7c-8676-dfc751855498",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x)=|x+6|-3,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-\\infty,-4]$\n- **II.** $x\\in [-4,\\infty)$\n- **III.** $x\\in (-\\infty,-6]$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The graph of the function $f(x)=|x+6|-3$ can be obtained in the following way:\n\n- Take the curve $y=|x|.$\n\n- Translate it by $6$ units to the left,  to get $y=|x+6|.$\n\n- Finally, translate $y=|x+6|$ by $3$ units down to get $f(x)=|x+6|-3.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186124474/plots/6f5cb8be5c1560234ca36173b5ff73f571de195c5f66c5f7e0be52597a58e493-0.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in (-\\infty,-6]$ and $x\\in [-4,\\infty).$ On these intervals, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186124474/plots/6f5cb8be5c1560234ca36173b5ff73f571de195c5f66c5f7e0be52597a58e493-1.png)\n\n  \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not invertible on the interval $x\\in (-\\infty,-4].$ On this interval, some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186124474/plots/6f5cb8be5c1560234ca36173b5ff73f571de195c5f66c5f7e0be52597a58e493-2.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\".",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "3fa6d4e1-eb42-53a0-a497-8c6941eccf8b",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
