  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186124474,
      "id": "149fa184-850f-52d8-a309-4b79a371a74d",
      "title": "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given a Description"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "6423c50b-c546-5db3-8d70-afca6e233685",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x)={x}^{2}+4,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-2,2)$\n- **II.** $x\\in [0,\\infty)$\n- **III.** $x\\in (-\\infty,0]$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The graph of the function $f(x)={x}^{2}+4$ can be obtained in the following way:\n\n- Take the curve $y={x}^{2}.$\n\n- Translate it by $4$ units up to get $f(x)={x}^{2}+4.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186124474/plots/750ebaca5c4c6365d86e86254848e0ed61a9a329715804cb379610a966beaa9c-0.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not invertible on the interval $x\\in (-2,2).$ On this interval, some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186124474/plots/750ebaca5c4c6365d86e86254848e0ed61a9a329715804cb379610a966beaa9c-1.png)\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is invertible on the intervals $x\\in [0,\\infty)$ and  $x\\in (-\\infty,0].$ On these intervals, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186124474/plots/750ebaca5c4c6365d86e86254848e0ed61a9a329715804cb379610a966beaa9c-2.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\".",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "0af46385-00ff-5575-9130-83cf871d5dca",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
