  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186124474,
      "id": "149fa184-850f-52d8-a309-4b79a371a74d",
      "title": "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given a Description"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "a0a364c8-2540-53fd-94be-54872c0ef975",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x)=(x+6)^{2},$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-6,-4]$\n- **II.** $x\\in (-7,-5]$\n- **III.** $x\\in (-6,\\infty)$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it is one-to-one on that interval.\n\nThe vertex occurs at $x=-6$. On either side of this vertex, the function is strictly monotone. Including the vertex as an endpoint does not create a repeated output. An interval containing points on both sides is not one-to-one: inputs equally far from the vertex have the same output.\n\n- Interval I, $(-6,-4]$, lies on one side of the vertex, since $-6\\ge -6$. It is therefore invertible.\n\n- Interval II, $(-7,-5]$, contains the distinct inputs $- \\frac{13}{2}$ and $- \\frac{11}{2}$, both with output $\\frac{1}{4}$. It is therefore not invertible.\n\n- Interval III, $(-6,\\infty)$, lies on one side of the vertex, since $-6\\ge -6$. It is therefore invertible.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\".",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "efeff453-2441-5d7d-bba0-c3261ec91097",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "33234f72-6b82-5bf1-a6cf-0ce46a2dbc09",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "cdf7400d-9a9e-5e27-adab-b244fd3c1ea9",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "cdf7400d-9a9e-5e27-adab-b244fd3c1ea9"
          ]
        },
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "b0cebe95-5cc7-5cd8-87ad-b873970575ac",
          ":answer-field/key": "II",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "ecbaeee8-9746-5e16-824f-b33f86ba86cf",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "1bb8afd1-a417-5525-bb12-49b1f24585c5",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "ecbaeee8-9746-5e16-824f-b33f86ba86cf"
          ]
        },
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "68e0f492-56b5-51a4-b5b9-a9d190ee52db",
          ":answer-field/key": "III",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
