  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186124474,
      "id": "149fa184-850f-52d8-a309-4b79a371a74d",
      "title": "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given a Description"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "2e7bfd6a-30c1-541a-bf79-2dea7612bde2",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x)=(x-3)^{2},$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (3,\\infty)$\n\n- **II.** $x\\in (0,6)$\n\n- **III.** $x\\in (-\\infty,3]$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The graph of the function $f(x)=(x-3)^{2},$ can be obtained in the following way:\n\n1\\. Take the curve $y={x}^{2}.$\n\n2\\. Translate it by $3$ units  to  the right  $f(x)=(x-3)^{2}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186124474/plots/09d8c784da84688c932d61e15265d33252ca0a58ba7583f1fca3bb35d208550e-0.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not invertible on the interval $x\\in (0,6).$ On this interval, some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186124474/plots/09d8c784da84688c932d61e15265d33252ca0a58ba7583f1fca3bb35d208550e-1.png)\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is invertible on the intervals $x\\in (3,\\infty)$  and $x\\in (-\\infty,3].$  On these intervals, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186124474/plots/09d8c784da84688c932d61e15265d33252ca0a58ba7583f1fca3bb35d208550e-2.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\".",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "5d5774e6-296f-5646-8d90-4db20e885f48",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
