  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186124474,
      "id": "149fa184-850f-52d8-a309-4b79a371a74d",
      "title": "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given a Description"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "fe01b252-58fb-5871-9caa-e02bfd14f651",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x)=|x+5|-5,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-\\infty,-3]$\n- **II.** $x\\in [-3,\\infty)$\n- **III.** $x\\in (-\\infty,-5]$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The graph of the function $f(x)=|x+5|-5$ can be obtained in the following way:\n\n- Take the curve $y=|x|.$\n\n- Translate it by $5$ units to the left,  to get $y=|x+5|.$\n\n- Finally, translate $y=|x+5|$ by $5$ units down to get $f(x)=|x+5|-5.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186124474/plots/b2d84aecec38a4ba62aeee57d8202c82fbacf593ff22278079693ec9e199f374-0.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in (-\\infty,-5]$ and $x\\in [-3,\\infty).$ On these intervals, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186124474/plots/b2d84aecec38a4ba62aeee57d8202c82fbacf593ff22278079693ec9e199f374-1.png)\n\n  \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not invertible on the interval $x\\in (-\\infty,-3].$ On this interval, some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186124474/plots/b2d84aecec38a4ba62aeee57d8202c82fbacf593ff22278079693ec9e199f374-2.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\".",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "18692512-4689-5c35-8b8d-0e3de79d4c5b",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
